Time Complexity (TC): O(4^n / √n)

Auxiliary Space Complexity (SC): O(n), excluding the output.

Output Space: O(n × 4^n / √n) = O(√n × 4^n)

Why?

- There are Cn = O(4^n / √n) valid parentheses combinations (Catalan number).
- Each combination has length 2n, so generating and storing all results takes O(n × Cn) time.
- The recursion depth and current string require O(n) auxiliary space.

Interview answer: TC = O(4^n / √n), auxiliary SC = O(n), excluding the output.


class Solution {
public:
    void solve(int n, int open,int close,string &curr,vector<string>&ans)
    {
        if(open == n && close == n)
        {
            ans.push_back(curr);
            return;
        }

        if(open < n)
        {
            curr.push_back('(');
            solve(n,open+1,close,curr,ans);
            curr.pop_back();
        }

        if(close < open)
        {
            curr.push_back(')');
            solve(n,open,close+1,curr,ans);
            curr.pop_back();
        }
    }
    vector<string> generateParenthesis(int n) {
        vector<string>ans;
        string curr = "";
        solve(n,0,0,curr,ans);
        return ans;
    }
};
